WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:05.600
No, no, no, no. What do we need at events?

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:08.600
People.

00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:14.800
We saw during the pandemic, so many people
were afraid that live events would not come back,

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:21.300
because it's more convenient to watch it online.
It's more convenient to watch it at your own pace.

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:27.200
But we as human beings are social creatures.

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:31.100
We desire that connection.
We desire that interaction.

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:36.900
We want to be there.
We want to feel the excitement.

00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:43.400
Can you imagine trying to get hyped before a
conference keynote session from your computer at home?

00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:48.800
Like the vibe in the general session room this morning.

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:57.000
It is much more difficult to create that level
of excitement, of hype, if they're not here together.

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:04.900
There is a term that we use in academia,
and it's called communitas.

00:01:04.900 --> 00:01:09.900
It means people coming together.

00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:17.200
There is a certain aspect of events that gives us the
opportunity to remove the barriers that keep us

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:20.900
separated in day-to-day lives.

00:01:20.900 --> 00:01:26.500
When you're standing in line to get one of the super
fancy yummy burgers in the exhibit hall,

00:01:26.500 --> 00:01:31.400
and you're just chatting somebody up, you're not
thinking about, oh, this is a CEO,

00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:36.400
or this is somebody that makes more money than me
or less money than me, or they don't have kids and I do.

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:38.900
You're not thinking about that.

00:01:38.900 --> 00:01:43.000
You are here in the moment,
enjoying the moment with other people.
